{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-04_exhibit991supplementalsche.htm, sha256 e39e026fae3522b6f8f407f304395c9a8333a9d1ad6c30bed14b2014b3a19e6c.\nEX-99.1 2 exhibit991supplementalsche.htm EX-99.1\nExhibit 99.1 Qnity Reports Third Quarter 2026 Results, Raises Full-Year Financial Guidance\n\u2013Third quarter Net Sales and Organic Sales(1) of $1.6 billion, up 22% year-over-year \u2013Gross Margin and Adjusted Gross Margin(1) of 47.8% \u2013GAAP Net Income of $196 million and Adjusted Operating EBITDA(1) of $503 million \u2013GAAP EPS of $0.87, down 14% year-over-year \u2013Adjusted EPS(1) of $1.46, up 55% year-over-year\nWILMINGTON, Del., November 4, 2026 \u2013 Qnity Electronics, Inc. (\u201cQnity\u201d) (NYSE: Q) today reported results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026.\n\u201cWe delivered our tenth consecutive quarter of profitable growth with strong performance across both segments as Qnity continues to establish itself as the premier solutions provider across the semiconductor value chain,\u201d said Jon Kemp, Qnity\u2019s Chief Executive Officer. \u201cA year of disciplined execution as an independent company shows what sets Qnity apart: a deep portfolio, close alignment with our customers' roadmaps, and a local-for-local model that delivers at scale.\u201d\nKemp added, \u201cMaterials innovation is quickly becoming a critical driver of chip performance as the industry shifts toward shrink and stack. Qnity\u2019s end-to-end solutions across the stack enable customers to address the most complex system level challenges: signal reliability, power density, and thermal management. We see tremendous opportunities ahead, and we\u2019re continuing to invest in differentiated technologies where we see visible customer demand to create significant value for our shareholders.\u201d\nFinancial Results Summary\nIn millions, except per share amounts GAAP Results\nQ3 2026 (1) Q3 2025 (2)\nNet Sales $1,556 $1,276\nSemiconductor Technologies 797 693\nInterconnect Solutions 759 583\nGross Profit $743 $575\nNet Income $196 $223\nDiluted Earnings Per Share $0.87 $1.01\nNon-GAAP Results\nAdjusted Gross Profit $743 $575\nAdjusted Operating EBITDA $503 $370\nAdjusted Earnings, net of tax $306 $197\nAdjusted Earnings Per Share $1.46 $0.94\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "(1) Organic Sales, Adjusted Gross Profit, Adjusted Gross Margin, Adjusted Operating EBITDA, Adjusted Operating EBITDA Margin, Adjusted Earnings, and Adjusted EPS are non-GAAP measures. See \u201cNon-GAAP Measures\u201d for further discussion, including a definition of significant items. Reconciliations to the most directly comparable GAAP measure, including details of significant items, can be found in the \u201cNon-GAAP Measures\u201d section of this press release. (2) Q3 2025 is presented on a pro forma basis. The pro forma non-GAAP measures give effect to pro forma adjustments related to interest expense associated with our current indebtedness, agreements executed in connection with the spin-off on November 1, 2025, from DuPont de Nemours, Inc. (\u201cDuPont\u201d) and other standalone costs as if the spin-off had occurred on January 1, 2025. See \u201cNon-GAAP Measures\u201d for further discussion, including a definition of significant items. Reconciliations to the most directly comparable GAAP measure, including details of significant items, can be found in the \u201cNon-GAAP Measures\u201d section of this press release. Refer to the \u201cNon-GAAP Measures\u201d section of this press release for further details on these adjustments.\nGuidance for Full Year 2026 Qnity is raising full\u2011year guidance based on strong third\u2011quarter performance and continued momentum in the business.\nQnity\u2019s full year 2026 guidance (3) is as follows:\nNet Sales $5.77B - $5.83B\nAdjusted Operating EBITDA $1.785B - $1.805B\nAdjusted EPS $4.95 - $5.05\nAdjusted Free Cash Flow $800M - $900M\n(3) We calculate forward-looking Adjusted Operating EBITDA, Adjusted EPS, and Adjusted Free Cash Flow based on internal forecasts that exclude certain information that would be included in the most directly comparable forward-looking GAAP measures. We are not providing a quantitative reconciliation of forward-looking Non-GAAP financial measures to the corresponding GAAP financial measure for these measures due to the unreasonable effort and uncertainty in estimating certain items necessary for such reconciliations, including adjustments that could be made for significant items, interest expense, indirect legacy costs/benefits, transformation, integration, and other charges, share-based compensation amounts, non-recurring, unusual or unanticipated charges, expenses or gains.\nConference Call and Webcast Information Qnity will hold a conference call to review these results on Wednesday, November 4, 2026, at 8:00 a.m. ET. Investors can join the conference call via telephone by dialing (800) 343-5172 (domestic) or +1 (203) 518-9856 (international) and using the participant code QNITY. An audio-only live webcast, presentation materials, and replay will also be made available at Events | Qnity Electronics, Inc. (Q).\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "About Qnity Qnity is a premier technology provider across the semiconductor value chain, empowering AI, high performance computing, and advanced connectivity. From groundbreaking solutions for semiconductor chip manufacturing, to enabling high-speed transmission within complex electronic systems, our high-performance materials and integration expertise make tomorrow\u2019s technologies possible. More information about Qnity, a constituent of the S&P 500 index, its businesses, and solutions can be found at http://www.qnityelectronics.com.\nQnity\u2122, the Qnity Node Logo, and all products, unless otherwise noted, denoted with TM or \u00ae are trademarks, trade names or registered trademarks of affiliates of Qnity Electronics, Inc.\n2\n"}
